## A CLOCK NOTE, BECAUSE IT NEARLY CAUSED A WRONG ROLLBACK

The first attempt at the "+15" read computed elapsed time with a PowerShell datetime subtraction
against a 'Z'-suffixed literal. It printed "+252.2 min" and "due yet: True" when only 12 minutes had
passed: the literal was taken as LOCAL and compared against a UTC value, a flat 240-minute error.
R4 had grown by 2 at that moment and needed 3. Had that reading been accepted, the order's step 8
would have rolled back a runner that was working perfectly.
**Every elapsed figure below is EPOCH arithmetic.** The real +15 read was taken at +17.9 min.

